            <ArticleTitle>The relationship of socioeconomic status to subsequent health status in systemic lupus erythematosus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>423-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We examined the relationship of socioeconomic status to health status, as determined by the Arthritis Impact Measurement Scales, in 78 systemic lupus erythematosus patients who had been entered into a prospective study. After controlling for age, disease duration, and disease severity, a significant relationship between socioeconomic status and outcome was not demonstrated. All study subjects had health insurance for medical services. The results have potential implications for health care policy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
